// Title: Invoke-Obfuscation Via Use Clip
// Sigma ID: e1561947-b4e3-4a74-9bdd-83baed21bdb5
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nikita Nazarov, oscd.community
// Date: 2020-10-09 | Modified: 2026-03-16
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1027, execution, T1059.001
// Description: Detects Obfuscated Powershell via use Clip.exe in Scripts
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/issues/1009
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_invoke_obfuscation_via_use_clip.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine matches regex "(?i)echo.*clip.*&&.*(?:Clipboard|i`?n`?v`?o`?k`?e`?)"
